# pkg/

Install-time artifacts intended for packaging on modern systemd-based distros (Debian 13+, Ubuntu 24.04+, RHEL 10+, CentOS Stream 10+, etc.).

## What’s included (common)

### sysusers.d
- `pkg/common/sysusers.d/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@.conf`
  - Creates:
    - system group `@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@`
    - system user `@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@` (home: `/home/@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@`, shell defaults to `/usr/sbin/nologin`)
  - Adds `@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@` to `@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@`

**Package install target:** `/usr/lib/sysusers.d/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@.conf`

### tmpfiles.d
- `pkg/common/tmpfiles.d/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@.conf`
  - Creates directories:
    - `/home/@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@` (0755 @CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@:@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@)
    - `/home/@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@/shared` (2775 @CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@:@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@, setgid)
    - `/home/@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@/tmp` (0700 @CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@:@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@)

**Package install target:** `/usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@.conf`

### sudoers drop-in
- `pkg/common/sudoers.d/@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@-echo`
  - Allows members of `@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@` to run `/usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/run-as-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@` as root without a password.
  - The wrapper executes an arbitrary command as user `@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@` inside a hardened transient systemd unit.

**Package install target:** `/etc/sudoers.d/@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@-@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@-echo`

## Admin: enrolling end-users

End-users must be added to `@CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@` to:
- access `/home/@CLI_SANDBOX_USERNAME@/shared/...` workspaces
- run the packaged sudoers-authorized wrapper command(s)

Example:

```bash
sudo usermod -a -G @CLI_SANDBOX_GROUPNAME@ <username>
# log out/in for group membership to take effect
```

## Notes

- `/usr/lib/...` is used for vendor-supplied sysusers/tmpfiles/systemd units. `/etc/...` is reserved for admin overrides.
- Packaging should ensure `/etc/sudoers.d/*` drop-ins are `root:root` and `0440`.
- Wrapper scripts under `/usr/libexec/@CLI_TOOL_NAME@/` should be `root:root` and executable.
